From: MCode <mcode@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] asoc: q6afe: arm the MI2S bit clock for the speaker port of lmi

The TFA9874 amplifier of this board is driven by a back end link ("no-pcm")
whose platform component is q6routing.  The sm8250 machine driver resolves
the CPU DAI of the runtime with snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(), which returns the
front end (q6asmdai) and not the q6afedai that owns the MI2S port, so its
PRIMARY_MI2S_RX case is never reached: the MI2S bit clock is never
programmed, its enable counter stays at 0, the amplifier never locks its
PLL and the speaker stays mute.

The clock is armed in the DAI, after the port configuration has been
applied and the port has been started, which is the position the machine
driver uses.  It is armed on every start and not only on the first one:
the port is stopped when the stream ends and the AFE can lose its clock
configuration, a system suspend for instance.  Arming it again is
idempotent.

The expected bit clock is computed from the parameters of the stream:
params_width() already returns a number of bits, so it is the rate times
the width times the number of channels, 48000 x 16 x 2 = 1536000 Hz, which
is the value the machine driver programs.  The value of the machine driver
is the one that is programmed, a difference is only reported.

When the clock cannot be armed, the port that was started just before is
stopped again and the port state is cleared, so the DAI and the AFE stay
in agreement.

Only the MI2S receive ports are concerned: the WCD938x codec, the
headset, the microphone and the USB audio keep the clock handling they
have.

Signed-off-by: MCode <mcode@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c | 106 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 100 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -17,6 +17,15 @@
 #include "q6afe.h"
 
 
+/*
+ * Bit clock of the MI2S ports of this board.  It is the value the sm8250
+ * machine driver programs for those ports (MI2S_BCLK_RATE in
+ * sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c): the back end links are forced to 48 kHz,
+ * 16 bit and two channels by sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(), that is
+ * 48000 x 16 x 2 = 1536000 Hz.
+ */
+#define Q6AFE_LMI_MI2S_BCLK_RATE	1536000
+
 struct q6afe_dai_priv_data {
 	uint32_t sd_line_mask;
 	uint32_t sync_mode;
@@ -384,11 +393,33 @@
 
 }
 
+/*
+ * Clock id of the bit clock of an MI2S receive port, -1 for the other ports.
+ * The transmit ports have no bit clock of their own: they are fed by the
+ * clock of the port they are coupled to.
+ */
+static int q6afe_dai_mi2s_clk_id(unsigned int dai_id)
+{
+	switch (dai_id) {
+	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX:
+		return Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_PRI_MI2S_IBIT;
+	case SECONDARY_MI2S_RX:
+		return Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_SEC_MI2S_IBIT;
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_RX:
+		return Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_TER_MI2S_IBIT;
+	case QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX:
+		return Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUAD_MI2S_IBIT;
+	default:
+		return -1;
+	}
+}
+
 static int q6afe_dai_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		struct snd_soc_dai *dai)
 {
 	struct q6afe_dai_data *dai_data = dev_get_drvdata(dai->dev);
 	int rc;
+	int clk_id;
 
 	if (dai_data->is_port_started[dai->id]) {
 		/* stop the port and restart with new port config */
@@ -443,6 +474,77 @@
 	}
 	dai_data->is_port_started[dai->id] = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * lmi: the back end link of the TFA9874 amplifier is a "no-pcm" link
+	 * whose platform component is q6routing, so the sm8250 machine driver
+	 * never reaches its PRIMARY_MI2S_RX case: it resolves the CPU DAI of
+	 * the runtime with snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(), which returns the front end
+	 * (q6asmdai) and not the q6afedai that owns the port.  The MI2S bit
+	 * clock is therefore never programmed (its enable counter stays at 0),
+	 * the TFA9874 never locks its PLL (PLLS = 0, CLKS falls back to 0) and
+	 * the speaker stays mute.
+	 *
+	 * The clock is armed here, that is after the port configuration has
+	 * been applied and the port has been started: this is the position
+	 * the machine driver uses (sm8250_snd_startup()), and the AFE derives
+	 * the bit clock from the port configuration.
+	 *
+	 * It is armed on every start, not only on the first one: the port is
+	 * stopped again when the stream ends, and the AFE can lose its clock
+	 * configuration, a system suspend for instance.  Arming the clock
+	 * again is idempotent.
+	 *
+	 * Only the MI2S receive ports are concerned: the other links of the
+	 * card (the WCD938x codec on the DMA ports, the headset, the
+	 * microphone, the USB audio) keep the clock handling they have.
+	 */
+	clk_id = q6afe_dai_mi2s_clk_id(dai->id);
+	if (clk_id >= 0) {
+		struct q6afe_i2s_cfg *i2s =
+			&dai_data->port_config[dai->id].i2s_cfg;
+		unsigned int bclk = Q6AFE_LMI_MI2S_BCLK_RATE;
+		unsigned int expected;
+
+		/*
+		 * The bit clock has to match the stream.  params_width() is
+		 * already a number of bits, so the expected bit clock is
+		 * rate x width x channels: 48000 x 16 x 2 = 1536000 Hz.
+		 * The machine driver forces those parameters on the back
+		 * end links, so the two agree; a difference is worth a
+		 * warning, but the value of the machine driver is the one
+		 * that is programmed.
+		 */
+		expected = i2s->sample_rate * i2s->bit_width *
+			   i2s->num_channels;
+		if (expected && expected != bclk)
+			dev_warn(dai->dev,
+				 "MI2S port %x: the stream asks for %u Hz, the machine driver programs %u Hz\n",
+				 dai->id, expected, bclk);
+
+		rc = q6afe_port_set_sysclk(dai_data->port[dai->id], clk_id,
+					   Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO,
+					   Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT,
+					   bclk, substream->stream);
+		if (rc) {
+			dev_err(dai->dev,
+				"Couldn't set the MI2S clock on port %x: %d\n",
+				dai->id, rc);
+			/*
+			 * The port has been started already: leave it in the
+			 * state it had before, otherwise the AFE keeps a
+			 * running port that the DAI does not know about.
+			 */
+			if (q6afe_port_stop(dai_data->port[dai->id]) < 0)
+				dev_err(dai->dev,
+					"fail to close AFE port %x\n", dai->id);
+			dai_data->is_port_started[dai->id] = false;
+			return rc;
+		}
+		dev_info(dai->dev,
+			 "MI2S port %x: bit clock %u Hz armed by the DAI\n",
+			 dai->id, bclk);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
